Scaling Limitations & Suggestions
4. Company Tier ceiling at 5
(docs/07_progression.md:14-29)

Once you're Legendary, there's no further company progression track.

Suggestion: Keep Tier 5 as the last named tier, but add internal prestige ranks within it (Legendary I → II → III…). Each rank requires escalating gold + contracts + a unique "story feat" (defeat a named boss, complete a legendary dungeon, etc.). Rewards unlock meta-level mechanics: sending three parties simultaneously, hiring hero trainers, unlocking faction-exclusive missions.

5. Enemy CR caps at 10 with "10+" as undefined
(docs/05_enemies.md:7-14)

The design only formally defines CR 1–10. Above that, "10+" is a placeholder. Heroes max at 10 dice too, so high-tier late-game becomes a pure numbers arms race with no design intent.

Suggestion: Define CR 11–20 with a new mechanic tier instead of just bigger pools:

CR 11–15 "Elite": 11–15 dice + one passive ability (e.g., regenerate 2 HP/round, immune to one damage type)
CR 16–20 "Mythic": 16–20 dice + two passives + one active ability (counter-attack, summon adds, shield phase)
This gives enemies qualitative complexity rather than just more dice, keeping fights interesting against veteran heroes.

MODERATE (creates a plateau, not a stop)
6. Reputation tracks cap at 100
(docs/03_economy.md:56-78)

Three tracks, all 0–100. Once maxed, there's no reputation-based tension or reward.

Suggestion: At 100, each track unlocks a Legendary Status tier that is losable. Holding 100 Street Reputation means powerful criminal factions try to co-opt or destroy you; holding 100 Public Reputation attracts noble intrigue. This creates late-game pressure without needing to inflate numbers — the cap becomes a pressure point, not a wall.

7. Carry capacity formula is bounded by stat caps
(docs/03_economy.md:162-166)

CON + ⌊STR÷2⌋ maxes at 15 AW when both stats are 10. Late-game legendary armor might be heavier or you may want heroes to carry more.

Suggestion: Add an Equipment Mastery trait (available via prestige or specific training) that grants +3 AW carry without changing stats. Also, introduce Masterwork versions of heavy armors that have the same protection but weigh 1 AW less — making late-game equipment upgrades meaningful beyond just "better stats."

8. HP formula hits a ceiling
(docs/02_heroes.md:87)

CON × 3 + class base — with CON capped at 10, HP tops out (e.g., Fighter: 30 + ~10 base = ~40 HP max). Enemy damage at high CR can easily exceed this, making fights very swingy.

Suggestion: Let prestige ranks grant flat HP bonuses (e.g., +5 HP per prestige rank). This is simpler than changing the formula and keeps CON relevant while allowing late-game survivability to grow.

9. Gold economy has no defined inflation control
(docs/03_economy.md:16-29)

Tier 5 income dwarfs expenses. There's no defined gold sink for the endgame, so gold becomes meaningless.

Suggestion: Introduce late-game gold sinks that scale with company tier:

Hero retirement funds (pay a hero to retire as a trainer — ongoing weekly salary)
Political bribes to maintain/restore reputation tracks
Fortress upgrades (Citadel extensions, armory improvements)
Legendary equipment commissioning (pay to craft a specific item, long time + high cost)
10. Loot weight shifts for high-tier dungeons are undefined
(docs/04_dungeons.md:128-134)

"Dungeon tier shifts weights upward" is stated but not quantified. Without a formula, this can't scale.

Suggestion: Define an explicit formula, e.g.: each dungeon tier above 1 shifts 5% from Common → Uncommon, 2% from Uncommon → Rare. Add a Tier 5+ dungeon category where Legendary drops reach 8–10%, making late-game dungeon selection meaningful.

SUMMARY TABLE
Limit	Severity	Suggested Solution
Hero level cap (10)	CRITICAL	Prestige ranks with trait unlocks instead of stat points
Stat cap (1–10)	CRITICAL	Bonus Dice layer for post-cap growth
HQ slots cap (30)	CRITICAL	HQ Tier 5 + Branch Offices
Company tier cap (5)	CRITICAL	Internal prestige ranks within Tier 5
Enemy CR cap (10+)	CRITICAL	Define CR 11–20 with qualitative mechanics
Reputation cap (100)	MODERATE	Cap becomes a pressure point with losable Legendary Status
Carry capacity bound	MODERATE	Equipment Mastery trait + Masterwork items
HP formula ceiling	MODERATE	Flat HP bonuses per prestige rank
Gold inflation	MODERATE	Scaling gold sinks per company tier
Loot weight undefined	MODERATE	Explicit formula per dungeon tier
The two most interconnected issues are the level cap and stat cap — solving those with the Prestige + Bonus Dice approach gives you a foundation that makes most of the other limits easier to extend naturally.